    "spots": [
        {
            "cell": [
                23,
                6
            ],
            "line": "Notches in the bark, a woodcutter's: one for every day he came. They stop at forty, and the fortieth is cut deeper than the rest.",
            "page": true
        },
        {
            "cell": [
                16,
                12
            ],
            "line": "Under the boulders, where the moss is thinnest, a child's shoe, very old, and words scratched in the stone: keep the quiet ways.",
            "page": true
        },
        {
            "cell": [
                24,
                15
            ],
            "line": "The barrow door was opened from inside. Whoever lay here walked out, and never touched the gold.",
            "page": true
        },
        {
            "cell": [
                15,
                11
            ],
            "line": "A ring of mossed boulders under the high boughs. Nothing has moved them in a long time."
        },
        {
            "cell": [
                4,
                4
            ],
            "line": "Light comes down through the canopy in shafts, and the dust hangs in it."
        },
        {
            "cell": [
                25,
                16
            ],
            "line": "Runes cut into the plinth: 'To those who seek the quiet ways, the earth yields her riches.'"
        },
        {
            "cell": [
                10,
                14
            ],
            "line": "A spring comes up out of the limestone into a clear pool, cold enough to ache."
        },
        {
            "cell": [
                24,
                6
            ],
            "line": "Notches cut into the sycamore bark by a woodcutter. They mark a cache."
        }
    ],
